==Latin==
[[File:Uncrossed gladius.jpg|thumb|gladius (sword)]]

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{der|la|cel-gau|*kladyos||sword}} (compare {{cog|sga|claideb||sword}}, from {{der|la|cel-pro|*kladiwos||sword}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*kelh₂-||to beat, break}}. Could possibly also be inherited. Cognate with {{cog|la|clādes}}, {{m|la|clāva}}, {{m|la|percellō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|eccl=yes}}
* {{audio|la-cls-gladius.ogg|Audio (Classical)|lang=la}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|gladius||gladiī|m|second}}

# [[sword]]
#: ''Mitte '''gladium''' in vaginam.''
#:: Put the '''sword''' into its sheath.
#: ''In '''gladium''' incumbere.''
#:: To fall on one's '''sword'''.
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} [[murder]], [[death]]
# a [[gladiatorial]] [[contest]]
# [[swordfish]]

